; Verisectorium Bounded Context — Ubiquitous Language Schema in UDON
; Drawn from ~/src/verisectorium/msc/notes/30-2026-11-19-model-in-a-nutshell-after-four-stores.md

|context[verisectorium] Core epistemic tracking domain for a Verisectorium store.

  ; --- Value Object Enums ---

  |enum[piece-kind] What a piece exists to carry; each kind says what can be asked of it.
    |claim        An assertion that follows from grounds or evidence.
    |rule         What a made thing or specification is meant to do.
    |definition   A term and its binding sense in the Ubiquitous Language.
    |decision     A choice made by someone with standing, on named grounds.
    |quote        Someone's verbatim words, located in a source.
    |restatement  Says what another piece says without adding a new claim.
    |question     An open inquiry; evidence against a piece puts a question to it.
    |check        A repeatable program or procedure that can be re-run.

  |enum[decision-how] What was actually done in deciding (never bare "decided").
    |ruling      The party with standing ruled after thought.
    |assented    Put to the steward by another mind, and they agreed.
    |lean        Current inclination, cheap to reconsider.
    |unobjected  Seen by someone with standing without objection.
    |inferred    A mind chose on what it took to be the steward's intent.
    |hole-close  A mind chose weakly to close an unspecified hole.
    |habit       Nobody chose; in force by habit.

  |enum[reliance-kind] Why one piece points at another.
    |for-truth    Relies on the target holding true.
    |restates     Restates the target without adding claims on top.
    |from-source  Derived or quoted from this source piece.
    |related      Marked as related and distinct; nothing relies along it.

  |enum[check-outcome] What a check found about a piece at an exact version.
    |confirmed  Evidence held against the piece's premises.
    |refuted    Evidence stood against the piece; puts an open question to it.

  ; --- Algebraic Sum Types (inline-record variants) ---

  |variant[attribution] In whose words a decision stands.
    |located
      :source   @piece
      :span     string
      :verbatim string
    |attributed-not-located
      :who      string
      :note     string?

  |variant[slot] An ordered entry in a canonical outline.
    |settled
      :piece    @piece.accepted
      :note     string?
    |on-approval
      :piece    @piece
      :note     string?

  |variant[act] What was done — recorded as fact, never detached status prose.
    |made
      :by       string
      :piece    @piece
      :at       string
    |checked
      :by       string
      :about    @piece
      :version  int
      :method   string
      :outcome  check-outcome
      :relies-on @piece*
      :at       string
      :main     string?
    |decided
      :by       string
      :about    @piece
      :how      decision-how
      :words    attribution
      :grounds  @piece*
      :at       string
    |reflected-in
      :by       string
      :piece    @piece
      :supersedes @piece?
      :at       string
    |knowingly-left
      :by       string
      :about    @piece
      :reopen-when string
      :at       string
      :main     string

  ; --- Value Object Records ---

  |record[reliance] A directional reliance edge from one piece to another.
    :kind   reliance-kind
    :target @piece
    :note   string?

  ; --- Entities (keyed with [id] -> typed abstract OCaml ID witnesses!) ---

  |entity[piece] A unit small enough to be right or wrong on its own.
    |trait-axis[standing]
      |draft     Suggested or in progress; not yet canonical for downstream readers.
      |accepted  Settled and answered-for in canonical outlines.
    |traits
      |repeatable     A check that can be re-run mechanically.
      |steward-words  Holds verbatim words of the steward.
      |derived        Derived from upstream decisions rather than chosen directly.
    :kind    piece-kind
    :author  string
    :version int
    :main    string
    |children
      |relies-on reliance
      |prose     @piece

  |entity[outline] An ordered gathering of pieces answered-for on behalf of a named reader.
    |trait-axis[scope]
      |working      For minds actively authoring; may reach on-approval slots.
      |deliverable  For downstream implementers/readers; requires accepted standing.
    :reader  string
    :main    string
    |children-ordered slot
